IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg11, Subchapter XVII:
-- section 388, "Domestication of non-United States entities".
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. It takes nobody's point of view; the seat layer dg11-seat.l4 asks these rules as questions.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (not the official text). `-- src:N | ...` is line N of it.
--
-- The section lets an entity formed under foreign law (a "non-United States entity") become a Delaware CORPORATION by DOMESTICATION: it files a
-- certificate of corporate domestication and a certificate of incorporation, and is then the same entity, now also a Delaware corporation.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE (taken as plain inputs, never recomputed):
--   * § 103 (piece dg1): that an instrument was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103, and the time it becomes effective, including a later effective date under § 103(d).
--   * § 106 (piece dg1): corporate existence ordinarily commences on the filing of the certificate of incorporation; subsection (d) displaces it "notwithstanding § 106".
--   * subchapter II (piece dg2): whether a corporate action is "within the power of a corporation under subchapter II" (subsection (m)).
--   * "applicable non-United States law" and the document governing the internal affairs of the non-United States entity: not among the inputs; whether an approval was given in the manner they provide is a BOOLEAN fact.
--   * the fee for the two certificates is § 391(a)(19) (this piece, dg11-s391-fees.l4).
-- The bracketed note in the heading ("For application of section, see 83 Del. Laws, c. 377, § 24") points to a session-law clause that is not in the text.

§ `Section 388(a) - definitions`

-- src:1939 | (1) “Foreign jurisdiction” means any foreign country or other foreign jurisdiction (other than the United States, any state, the District of Columbia, or any possession or territory of the United States); and
-- Gloss: the core's `Where an entity is formed` has three leaves; only `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` is a "foreign jurisdiction" in this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(a)(1) (src:1939)
GIVEN place IS A `Where an entity is formed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 388(a)(1) the place is a foreign jurisdiction` place MEANS
    place EQUALS `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`

-- src:1940 | (2) “Non-United States entity” means a corporation, a limited liability company, a statutory trust, a business trust or association, a real estate investment trust, a common-law trust, or any other unincorporated business or entity, including a partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), formed, incorporated, created or that otherwise came into being under the laws of any foreign jurisdiction.
-- Gloss: every kind of entity the core lists, except a natural person, if it was formed under the laws of a foreign jurisdiction. The core's `a joint-stock association` is "any other unincorporated business or entity". (Fork register F-388-1)
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(a)(2) (src:1940)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entity`
      place IS A `Where an entity is formed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` kind place MEANS
        (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a natural person` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND `s 388(a)(1) the place is a foreign jurisdiction` place

§ `Section 388(b), (g), (h) - how a non-United States entity becomes domesticated`

-- src:1941 | (b) Any non-United States entity may become domesticated as a corporation in this State by complying with subsection (h) of this section and filing with the Secretary of State:
-- src:1942 | (1) A certificate of corporate domestication which shall be executed in accordance with subsection (g) of this section and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title; and
-- src:1943 | (2) A certificate of incorporation, which shall be executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103 of this title.
-- src:1944 | Each of the certificates required by this subsection (b) shall be filed simultaneously with the Secretary of State and, if such certificates are not to become effective upon their filing as permitted by § 103(d) of this title, then each such certificate shall provide for the same effective date or time in accordance with § 103(d) of this title.
-- Gloss: the entity's power to become a Delaware corporation; the Secretary of State's correlative liability to accept the filing (an official: no seat).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(b) (src:1941-1944)
DECLARE `s 388(b) Filing with the Secretary of State` HAS
    `certificate of corporate domestication executed in accordance with subsection (g)`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `certificate of corporate domestication filed in accordance with § 103`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `certificate of incorporation executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the two certificates are filed simultaneously with the Secretary of State`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificates are to become effective upon their filing, as § 103(d) permits`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `each certificate provides for the same effective date or time in accordance with § 103(d)`      IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(b) (src:1941-1944)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of entity`
      place IS A `Where an entity is formed`
      `the entity has complied with subsection (h)` IS A BOOLEAN
      filing IS A `s 388(b) Filing with the Secretary of State`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 388(b) the non-United States entity may become domesticated as a corporation in this State` kind place `the entity has complied with subsection (h)` filing MEANS
        `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` kind place
    AND `the entity has complied with subsection (h)`
    AND filing's `certificate of corporate domestication executed in accordance with subsection (g)`
    AND filing's `certificate of corporate domestication filed in accordance with § 103`
    AND filing's `certificate of incorporation executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103`
    AND filing's `the two certificates are filed simultaneously with the Secretary of State`
    AND (    filing's `the certificates are to become effective upon their filing, as § 103(d) permits`
          OR filing's `each certificate provides for the same effective date or time in accordance with § 103(d)`)

-- src:1955 | (g) The certificate of corporate domestication shall be signed by any person who is authorized to sign the certificate of corporate domestication on behalf of the non-United States entity.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(g) (src:1955)
GIVEN `the person is authorized to sign the certificate of corporate domestication on behalf of the non-United States entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 388(g) the person may sign the certificate of corporate domestication` `the person is authorized to sign the certificate of corporate domestication on behalf of the non-United States entity` MEANS
    `the person is authorized to sign the certificate of corporate domestication on behalf of the non-United States entity`

-- src:1956 | (h) Prior to the time a certificate of corporate domestication becomes effective in accordance with § 103 of this title, the domestication shall be approved in the manner provided for by the document, instrument, agreement or other writing, as the case may be, governing the internal affairs of the non-United States entity and the conduct of its business or by applicable non-United States law, as appropriate, and the certificate of incorporation shall be approved by the same authorization required to approve the domestication.
-- Gloss: approval is given BEFORE the certificate of corporate domestication becomes effective, in the manner the governing document or the applicable non-United States law provides; the certificate of incorporation needs the SAME authorization.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(h) (src:1956)
GIVEN `the domestication has been approved in the manner provided for by the governing document or by applicable non-United States law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approval was given before the certificate of corporate domestication became effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation has been approved by the same authorization required to approve the domestication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 388(h) the domestication has been approved as required` `the domestication has been approved in the manner provided for by the governing document or by applicable non-United States law` `the approval was given before the certificate of corporate domestication became effective` `the certificate of incorporation has been approved by the same authorization required to approve the domestication` MEANS
        `the domestication has been approved in the manner provided for by the governing document or by applicable non-United States law`
    AND `the approval was given before the certificate of corporate domestication became effective`
    AND `the certificate of incorporation has been approved by the same authorization required to approve the domestication`

§ `Section 388(c) - what the certificate of corporate domestication certifies`

-- src:1945 | (c) The certificate of corporate domestication shall certify:
-- src:1946 | (1) The date on which and jurisdiction where the non-United States entity was first formed, incorporated, created or otherwise came into being;
-- src:1947 | (2) The name of the non-United States entity immediately prior to the filing of the certificate of corporate domestication;
-- src:1948 | (3) The name of the corporation as set forth in its certificate of incorporation filed in accordance with subsection (b) of this section;
-- src:1949 | (4) The jurisdiction that constituted the seat, siege social, or principal place of business or central administration of the non-United States entity or any other equivalent thereto under applicable law, immediately prior to the filing of the certificate of corporate domestication;
-- src:1950 | (5) That the domestication shall be approved prior to the effectiveness of such certificate in the manner provided for by the document, instrument, agreement or other writing, as the case may be, governing the internal affairs of the non-United States entity and the conduct of its business or by applicable non-United States law, as appropriate; and
-- src:1951 | (6) If a plan of domestication is adopted in accordance with subsection (l) of this section, that all provisions of the plan of domestication shall be approved prior to the effectiveness of such certificate in accordance with all applicable non-United States law, including any approval required under non-United States law for the authorization of the type of corporate action specified in the plan of domestication.
-- Gloss: (1) to (5) always; (6) only if a plan of domestication is adopted under subsection (l).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(c) (src:1945-1951)
DECLARE `s 388(c) What the certificate of corporate domestication certifies` HAS
    `date on which and jurisdiction where the non-United States entity was first formed, incorporated, created or otherwise came into being`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `name of the non-United States entity immediately prior to the filing of the certificate`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `name of the corporation as set forth in its certificate of incorporation`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `jurisdiction that constituted its seat, siege social, or principal place of business or central administration, immediately prior to the filing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that the domestication shall be approved prior to the effectiveness of the certificate in the manner provided for`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `that all provisions of the plan of domestication shall be approved prior to the effectiveness of the certificate`                        IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(c) (src:1945-1951)
GIVEN certifies IS A `s 388(c) What the certificate of corporate domestication certifies`
      `a plan of domestication is adopted in accordance with subsection (l)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 388(c) the certificate of corporate domestication certifies everything that subsection (c) requires` certifies `a plan of domestication is adopted in accordance with subsection (l)` MEANS
        certifies's `date on which and jurisdiction where the non-United States entity was first formed, incorporated, created or otherwise came into being`
    AND certifies's `name of the non-United States entity immediately prior to the filing of the certificate`
    AND certifies's `name of the corporation as set forth in its certificate of incorporation`
    AND certifies's `jurisdiction that constituted its seat, siege social, or principal place of business or central administration, immediately prior to the filing`
    AND certifies's `that the domestication shall be approved prior to the effectiveness of the certificate in the manner provided for`
    AND ((NOT `a plan of domestication is adopted in accordance with subsection (l)`)
         OR certifies's `that all provisions of the plan of domestication shall be approved prior to the effectiveness of the certificate`)

§ `Section 388(d) to (f) - when the domestication takes effect, and what it leaves unaffected`

-- src:1952 | (d) Upon the certificate of corporate domestication and the certificate of incorporation becoming effective in accordance with § 103 of this title, the non-United States entity shall be domesticated as a corporation in this State and the corporation shall thereafter be subject to all of the provisions of this title, except that notwithstanding § 106 of this title, the existence of the corporation shall be deemed to have commenced on the date the non-United States entity commenced its existence in the jurisdiction in which the non-United States entity was first formed, incorporated, created or otherwise came into being.
-- Gloss: on both certificates becoming effective, the entity IS domesticated as a Delaware corporation, and the corporation is thereafter subject to all of this title; but its existence is deemed to have commenced on the date the entity first came into being abroad,
-- not on the filing (the exception to § 106, piece dg1). The two certificates are inputs because the time at which each becomes effective is § 103(d) (piece dg1).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(d) (src:1952)
GIVEN `the certificate of corporate domestication has become effective in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation has become effective in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 388(d) the non-United States entity is domesticated as a corporation in this State, and the corporation is subject to all of the provisions of this title` `the certificate of corporate domestication has become effective in accordance with § 103` `the certificate of incorporation has become effective in accordance with § 103` MEANS
        `the certificate of corporate domestication has become effective in accordance with § 103`
    AND `the certificate of incorporation has become effective in accordance with § 103`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(d) (src:1952)
GIVEN `the entity is domesticated as a corporation in this State under subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the non-United States entity commenced its existence in the jurisdiction where it was first formed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 388(d) the date on which the existence of the corporation is deemed to have commenced` `the entity is domesticated as a corporation in this State under subsection (d)` `the date on which the non-United States entity commenced its existence in the jurisdiction where it was first formed` MEANS
    IF   `the entity is domesticated as a corporation in this State under subsection (d)`
    THEN JUST `the date on which the non-United States entity commenced its existence in the jurisdiction where it was first formed`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1953 | (e) The domestication of any non-United States entity as a corporation in this State shall not be deemed to affect any obligations or liabilities of the non-United States entity incurred prior to its domestication as a corporation in this State, or the personal liability of any person therefor.
-- Gloss: the domestication does not affect (i) an obligation or liability of the entity incurred prior to the domestication, or (ii) the personal liability of any person for it. Anything else is not addressed, so NOTHING.
-- The other side of the same relation: a creditor keeps the claim; a person liable keeps the liability.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(e) (src:1953)
DECLARE `s 388(e) Matter that the domestication leaves unaffected` IS ONE OF
    `an obligation or liability of the non-United States entity incurred prior to its domestication as a corporation in this State`
    `the personal liability of a person for such an obligation or liability`
    `another matter that s 388(e) does not name`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(e) (src:1953)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 388(e) Matter that the domestication leaves unaffected`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(e) the domestication leaves the matter unaffected` matter MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `another matter that s 388(e) does not name` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1954 | (f) The filing of a certificate of corporate domestication shall not affect the choice of law applicable to the non-United States entity, except that, from the effective time of the domestication, the law of the State of Delaware, including this title, shall apply to the non-United States entity to the same extent as if the non-United States entity had been incorporated as a corporation of this State on that date.
-- Gloss: the filing does not change the choice of law that applied to the entity; but FROM THE EFFECTIVE TIME the law of Delaware, including this title, applies to it as if it had been incorporated here on that date.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(f) (src:1954)
DECLARE `s 388(f) Law that applies to the non-United States entity` IS ONE OF
    `the choice of law that applied to it before the filing, unaffected by the filing`
    `the law of the State of Delaware, including this title, as if it had been incorporated as a corporation of this State on that date`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(f) (src:1954)
GIVEN `the time in question is at or after the effective time of the domestication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 388(f) Law that applies to the non-United States entity`
`s 388(f) the law that applies to the entity at the time in question` `the time in question is at or after the effective time of the domestication` MEANS
    IF   `the time in question is at or after the effective time of the domestication`
    THEN `the law of the State of Delaware, including this title, as if it had been incorporated as a corporation of this State on that date`
    ELSE `the choice of law that applied to it before the filing, unaffected by the filing`


§ `Section 388(i), (j) - the domesticated corporation is the same entity`

-- src:1957 | (i) When a non-United States entity has become domesticated as a corporation pursuant to this section, for all purposes of the laws of the State of Delaware, the corporation shall be deemed to be the same entity as the domesticating non-United States entity and the domestication shall constitute a continuation of the existence of the domesticating non-United States entity in the form of a corporation of this State. …
-- Gloss: for all purposes of Delaware law the corporation is the SAME entity as the domesticating entity, and the domestication is a CONTINUATION of the entity's existence in the form of a corporation of this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(i) (src:1957)
GIVEN `the domestication has become effective under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(i) the corporation is deemed to be the same entity as the domesticating non-United States entity, a continuation of its existence` `the domestication has become effective under this section` MEANS
    IF   `the domestication has become effective under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1957 | When any domestication shall have become effective under this section, for all purposes of the laws of the State of Delaware, all of the rights, privileges and powers of the non-United States entity that has been domesticated, and all property, real, personal and mixed, and all debts due to such non-United States entity, as well as all other things and causes of action belonging to such non-United States entity, shall remain vested in the corporation to which such non-United States entity has been domesticated (and also in the non-United States entity, if and for so long as the non-United States entity continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication) and shall be the property of such corporation (and also of the non-United States entity, if and for so long as the non-United States entity continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication), and the title to any real property vested by deed or otherwise in such non-United States entity shall not revert or be in any way impaired by reason of this title; but all rights of creditors and all liens upon any property of such non-United States entity shall be preserved unimpaired, and all debts, liabilities and duties of the non-United States entity that has been domesticated shall remain attached to the corporation to which such non-United States entity has been domesticated (and also to the non-United States entity, if and for so long as the non-United States entity continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication), and may be enforced against it to the same extent as if said debts, liabilities and duties had originally been incurred or contracted by it in its capacity as such corporation. …
-- Gloss: once effective, for all purposes of Delaware law: the rights, privileges, powers, property, debts due and causes of action of the entity remain vested in the corporation (and also in the entity, if and for so long as the entity continues
-- its existence in the foreign jurisdiction); title to real property does not revert or become impaired; creditors' rights and liens are preserved unimpaired; debts, liabilities and duties remain attached to the corporation (and also to the entity, if and for so long as it
-- continues) and may be enforced against it as if incurred by it as the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(i) (src:1957)
DECLARE `s 388(i) Who holds or bears after the domestication` IS ONE OF
    `the corporation alone`
    `the corporation and also the non-United States entity, if and for so long as it continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(i) (src:1957)
GIVEN `the domestication has become effective under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the non-United States entity continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 388(i) Who holds or bears after the domestication`
`s 388(i) in whom the rights, privileges, powers, property, debts due and causes of action of the non-United States entity remain vested` `the domestication has become effective under this section` `the non-United States entity continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication` MEANS
    IF   `the domestication has become effective under this section`
    THEN JUST (IF `the non-United States entity continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication`
               THEN `the corporation and also the non-United States entity, if and for so long as it continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication`
               ELSE `the corporation alone`)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(i) (src:1957)
GIVEN `the domestication has become effective under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the non-United States entity continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 388(i) Who holds or bears after the domestication`
`s 388(i) to whom the debts, liabilities and duties of the non-United States entity remain attached, to be enforced as if incurred by it as the corporation` `the domestication has become effective under this section` `the non-United States entity continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication` MEANS
    IF   `the domestication has become effective under this section`
    THEN JUST (IF `the non-United States entity continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication`
               THEN `the corporation and also the non-United States entity, if and for so long as it continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to the domestication`
               ELSE `the corporation alone`)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(i) (src:1957)
GIVEN `the domestication has become effective under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(i) title to real property vested in the non-United States entity reverts or is impaired by reason of this title` `the domestication has become effective under this section` MEANS
    IF   `the domestication has become effective under this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(i) (src:1957)
GIVEN `the domestication has become effective under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(i) the rights of creditors and the liens upon the property of the non-United States entity are preserved unimpaired` `the domestication has become effective under this section` MEANS
    IF   `the domestication has become effective under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1957 | The rights, privileges, powers and interests in property of the non-United States entity, as well as the debts, liabilities and duties of the non-United States entity, shall not be deemed, as a consequence of the domestication, to have been transferred to the corporation to which such non-United States entity has domesticated for any purpose of the laws of the State of Delaware.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(i) (src:1957)
GIVEN `the vesting or attaching results from the domestication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(i) the rights, privileges, powers, interests in property, debts, liabilities and duties are deemed to have been transferred to the corporation` `the vesting or attaching results from the domestication` MEANS
    IF   `the vesting or attaching results from the domestication`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1958 | (j) Unless otherwise agreed or otherwise required under applicable non-United States law, the domesticating non-United States entity shall not be required to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets, and the domestication shall not be deemed to constitute a dissolution of such non-United States entity. …
-- Gloss: unless the parties have otherwise agreed or applicable non-United States law otherwise requires, the entity need not wind up and the domestication is not a dissolution of it. The "unless" is read as qualifying both limbs
-- (Fork register F-388-2). If it is displaced, the text does not say what follows, so NOTHING.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(j) (src:1958)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `applicable non-United States law otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(j) the domestication requires the domesticating non-United States entity to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets` `it is otherwise agreed` `applicable non-United States law otherwise requires` MEANS
    IF   (NOT `it is otherwise agreed`) AND (NOT `applicable non-United States law otherwise requires`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(j) (src:1958)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `applicable non-United States law otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(j) the domestication is deemed to constitute a dissolution of the non-United States entity` `it is otherwise agreed` `applicable non-United States law otherwise requires` MEANS
    IF   (NOT `it is otherwise agreed`) AND (NOT `applicable non-United States law otherwise requires`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1958 | If, following domestication, a non-United States entity that has become domesticated as a corporation of this State continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to domestication, the corporation and such non-United States entity shall, for all purposes of the laws of the State of Delaware, constitute a single entity formed, incorporated, created or otherwise having come into being, as applicable, and existing under the laws of the State of Delaware and the laws of such foreign jurisdiction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(j) (src:1958)
GIVEN `the entity, following domestication, continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to domestication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(j) the corporation and the non-United States entity constitute a single entity` `the entity, following domestication, continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to domestication` MEANS
    IF   `the entity, following domestication, continues its existence in the foreign jurisdiction in which it was existing immediately prior to domestication`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 388(k), (l), (m) - interests, the plan of domestication, and corporate actions in the plan`

-- src:1959 | (k) In connection with a domestication under this section, shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, the non-United States entity that is to be domesticated as a corporation of this State may be exchanged for or converted into cash, property, or shares of stock, rights or securities of such corporation or, in addition to or in lieu thereof, may be exchanged for or converted into cash, property, or shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, another corporation or other entity or may be cancelled.
-- Gloss: in connection with the domestication, shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, the non-United States entity MAY be exchanged for or converted into cash, property, or shares, rights or securities of the corporation,
-- or (in addition or in lieu) of, or interests in, another corporation or other entity, or MAY be cancelled. Any other treatment is not addressed, so NOTHING. The holder's side: the interest is subject to this power (a liability).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(k) (src:1959)
DECLARE `s 388(k) Treatment of the shares, rights, securities or interests of the non-United States entity` IS ONE OF
    `exchanged for or converted into cash in a domestication`
    `exchanged for or converted into property in a domestication`
    `exchanged for or converted into shares of stock, rights or securities of the corporation in a domestication`
    `exchanged for or converted into cash, property, or shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, another corporation or other entity in a domestication`
    `cancelled in a domestication`
    `treated in a way that s 388(k) does not name`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(k) (src:1959)
GIVEN treatment IS A `s 388(k) Treatment of the shares, rights, securities or interests of the non-United States entity`
      `it is in connection with a domestication under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(k) the shares, rights, securities or interests may be so treated` treatment `it is in connection with a domestication under this section` MEANS
    IF   `it is in connection with a domestication under this section`
    THEN CONSIDER treatment
         WHEN `treated in a way that s 388(k) does not name` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1960 | (l) In connection with a domestication under this section, a non-United States entity may adopt a plan of domestication that may state: (i) the terms and conditions of the domestication, (ii) the mode of carrying the same into effect, (iii) that the certificate of incorporation of the domesticated corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the plan of domestication, (iv) the manner, if any, of exchanging or converting shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, the non-United States entity that is to be domesticated as a corporation of this State, in accordance with subsection (k) of this section, (v) any corporate action to be taken by the domesticated corporation of this State in connection with the domestication of the non-United States entity, each of which shall require approval in accordance with all applicable non-United States law, including any approval required under non-United States law for the authorization of the type of corporate action specified in the plan of domestication; (vi) any details or provisions as are deemed desirable, and (vii) such other provisions or facts as shall be required to be set forth in a plan of domestication by the laws of the jurisdiction under which the non-United States entity is organized. …
-- Gloss: the entity may adopt a plan of domestication that may state any of (i) to (vii). Item (v), any corporate action to be taken by the domesticated corporation in connection with the domestication, "shall require approval in accordance with all
-- applicable non-United States law, including any approval required under non-United States law for the authorization of the type of corporate action specified in the plan".
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(l) (src:1960)
DECLARE `s 388(l) Statement that a plan of domestication may make` IS ONE OF
    `the terms and conditions of the domestication`
    `the mode of carrying the same into effect`
    `that the certificate of incorporation of the domesticated corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the plan of domestication`
    `the manner, if any, of exchanging or converting shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, the non-United States entity, in accordance with subsection (k)`
    `any corporate action to be taken by the domesticated corporation of this State in connection with the domestication`
    `any details or provisions as are deemed desirable`
    `such other provisions or facts as shall be required by the laws of the jurisdiction under which the non-United States entity is organized`
    `a statement that s 388(l) does not list`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(l) (src:1960)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 388(l) Statement that a plan of domestication may make`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(l) the plan of domestication may state it` statement MEANS
    CONSIDER statement
    WHEN `a statement that s 388(l) does not list` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(l) (src:1960)
GIVEN `the corporate action has been approved in accordance with all applicable non-United States law, including any approval required for the type of corporate action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 388(l)(v) the corporate action stated in the plan may be taken` `the corporate action has been approved in accordance with all applicable non-United States law, including any approval required for the type of corporate action` MEANS
    `the corporate action has been approved in accordance with all applicable non-United States law, including any approval required for the type of corporate action`

-- src:1960 | Any of the terms of the plan of domestication may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of such plan, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the terms of the plan of domestication is clearly and expressly set forth in the plan of domestication. …
-- Gloss: a term may depend on facts outside the plan only if the manner in which those facts operate on the terms is clearly and expressly set forth in the plan.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(l) (src:1960)
GIVEN `the manner in which the facts operate upon the terms of the plan of domestication is clearly and expressly set forth in the plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 388(l) a term of the plan of domestication may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of the plan` `the manner in which the facts operate upon the terms of the plan of domestication is clearly and expressly set forth in the plan` MEANS
    `the manner in which the facts operate upon the terms of the plan of domestication is clearly and expressly set forth in the plan`

-- src:1960 | The term “facts,” as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the non-United States entity or the domesticated corporation.
-- Gloss: in the preceding sentence "facts" includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, and a determination or action by any person or body, including the non-United States entity or the domesticated corporation.
-- The list is "not limited to", so a fact of another kind is not shown NOT to be one: NOTHING (not covered). (Fork register F-388-4)
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(l) (src:1960)
DECLARE `s 388(l) Kind of fact on which a term of the plan may depend` IS ONE OF
    `the occurrence of any event`
    `a determination or action by any person or body, including the non-United States entity or the domesticated corporation`
    `a fact of another kind that s 388(l) does not name`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(l) (src:1960)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 388(l) Kind of fact on which a term of the plan may depend`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(l) the fact is a fact within the meaning of the preceding sentence` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a fact of another kind that s 388(l) does not name` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1961 | (m) Any corporate action to be taken by the domesticated corporation of this State in connection with the domestication of the non-United States entity that is set forth in a plan of domestication approved in the manner provided for by subsection (l) of this section and that is within the power of a corporation under subchapter II of this chapter shall be deemed authorized, adopted and approved, as applicable, by the domesticated corporation of this State and the board of directors, stockholders or members of the corporation, as applicable, and shall not require any further action of the board of directors, stockholders or members of the corporation under this title. …
-- Gloss: a corporate action set forth in a plan of domestication approved in the manner provided for by subsection (l), and within the power of a corporation under subchapter II (piece dg2), is DEEMED authorized, adopted and approved by the
-- domesticated corporation and by its board of directors, stockholders or members, and needs no further action of them under this title. The text's reference to approval "in the manner provided for by subsection (l)" is taken as a fact the caller states
-- (Fork register F-388-3).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(m) (src:1961)
GIVEN `the action is set forth in a plan of domestication approved in the manner provided for by subsection (l)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is within the power of a corporation under subchapter II of this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 388(m) the action is deemed authorized, adopted and approved, and needs no further action of the board of directors, stockholders or members under this title` `the action is set forth in a plan of domestication approved in the manner provided for by subsection (l)` `the action is within the power of a corporation under subchapter II of this chapter` MEANS
    IF   `the action is set forth in a plan of domestication approved in the manner provided for by subsection (l)`
         AND `the action is within the power of a corporation under subchapter II of this chapter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1961 | In the event that any such action requires the filing of a certificate under any other section of this title, the certificate shall state that in accordance with this section, no action by the board of directors, stockholders, members or as otherwise required by such other section of this title is required.
-- Gloss: where such an action requires a certificate under another section, the certificate shall state that, in accordance with this section, no action by the board of directors, stockholders, members or as otherwise required by that other section is required.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 388(m) (src:1961)
GIVEN `the action requires the filing of a certificate under another section of this title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that in accordance with this section no action is required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 388(m) the certificate meets the requirement of the last sentence of subsection (m)` `the action requires the filing of a certificate under another section of this title` `the certificate states that in accordance with this section no action is required` MEANS
    (NOT `the action requires the filing of a certificate under another section of this title`) OR `the certificate states that in accordance with this section no action is required`
